{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775208371,"nonce":"7bagndYpoUC6pXNEI2we9OFnBv0=","title":"Add support for different agent kinds for development (coder) and review steps, with a finetuning feedback loop.","message":"Use a simpler/cheaper agent for development and an expensive agent for review. Use review results to finetune the simpler agent over time.\n\n\n- WORKFLOW.md `agent.kind` controls the coder agent (already works)\n- REVIEW.md already has its own YAML front matter — add `agent.kind` there to control the review agent independently\n- Example: `agent.kind: openhands` in WORKFLOW.md (cheap coder), `agent.kind: claude-code` in REVIEW.md (expensive reviewer)\n\n- Review verdicts (approve/revise with comments) are structured training signal\n- Checkpoint/conversation logs in `/session/` provide full traces\n- Extract (prompt, agent_output, review_feedback) tuples for training data\n- Add a `nightshift export-training-data` command or similar\n\n- Cheaper agents may need higher `max_resumes` (hit context limits faster)\n- `max_turns` may also need per-step configuration\n- REVIEW.md agent may need different `stall_timeout_s` than WORKFLOW.md agent\n- Review step already has separate container naming (`nightshift-review-\u003cid\u003e`) and session handling\n\n1. Support `agent.kind` in REVIEW.md front matter (parse + use in review container launch)\n2. Allow per-step `max_turns` and `stall_timeout_s` overrides\n3. Add training data export from session logs (conversation.jsonl + review verdicts)\n4. Document the dual-agent workflow in CLAUDE.md\n\nREQ: new REQ (multi-agent workflow with finetuning loop)","files":null}]}